#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-portal: Hearth Files as every app's file chooser, and as the file manager other apps open.

  hearth-portal filechooser             the xdg-desktop-portal FileChooser backend, D-Bus name
                                        org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.hearth (started by D-Bus; hearth.portal and
                                        nimbus-portals.conf send xdg-desktop-portal's OpenFile / SaveFile / SaveFiles here)
  hearth-portal filemanager1 [--replace]   org.freedesktop.FileManager1: ShowFolders, ShowItems, ShowItemProperties
                                        ("Show in folder" / "Open containing folder" in Firefox, Chromium and Electron
                                        apps, Steam, GTK and Qt apps). Started by nimbus-session in both modes, so it holds
                                        the name before Dolphin, Nautilus or Thunar could be started for it.
  hearth-portal show PATH [--props]     Hearth Files at PATH (a file: its folder with it picked; --props: its Properties)
  hearth-portal pick REQUEST.json       the picker for a request (as the portal builds it); prints what was picked

How the window opens: in Desktop Mode, ShowFolders and friends use the desktop's own Hearth Files (quickshell ipc).
The picker, and Hearth Files in Game Mode, are picker.qml: Hearth Files (FileManager.qml) in its own Quickshell
window. In Game Mode (gamescope) that window is pinned in front (GAMESCOPECTRL_BASELAYER_WINDOW, the way Hearth shows
Steam's questions) and gets the controller through its own hearth-pad; Game Mode's controller mouse waits meanwhile.
Which mode is on comes from the session's activation environment (systemctl --user show-environment): Desktop Mode's
labwc puts WAYLAND_DISPLAY there, Game Mode's nimbus-watchdog DISPLAY with an empty WAYLAND_DISPLAY.

The picker gets a request file (HEARTH_PICK_REQUEST, JSON) and writes what was picked to HEARTH_PICK_RESULT:
  request: {kind: open|save|savefiles, title, accept, multiple, directory, filters: [{name, globs, mimes}], filter,
            folder, name, files, choices: [{id, label, options: [[id, label]], value}], app}
  result:  {paths: [...], filter: N, choices: {id: value}}   or   {cancel: true}
"""
